# Build context for the API image. Its context is the repo root, because `noa-api` is a
# uv workspace member and `noa-core` is the workspace root — see `apps/api/Dockerfile`.
#
# Two entries here are load-bearing rather than housekeeping:
#   * `.env` and friends — no secrets in git; an image layer is just as permanent and
#     rather harder to inspect. The API takes its configuration from the environment at boot.
#   * the two web packages — separate deploy artifacts with their own contexts.
#     Excluding them means the API image physically cannot pick up a file from either one.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Separate deploy artifacts ---
apps/admin-web/
apps/web-embed/

# --- Not part of any image ---
.git/
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml
apps/api/tests/
docs/
spikes/
tmp/
.artifacts/

# --- Local build/tooling output ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
node_modules/
*.log

# --- Editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.mcp.json
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docker's own files (never needed inside an image) ---
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
